<p>The architecture is straightforward. Your application makes parallel HTTP POST requests to the nine endpoints. Each request passes through the same gateway for authentication, rate limiting, and proxy routing. The rendering layer fetches the page in a headless Chrome instance (or a lightweight HTML parser for simpler endpoints), runs the analysis, and returns structured JSON.</p>

<p>The critical design choice: each endpoint is an independent call that fetches the page itself. Calling them in parallel rather than one after another keeps the wall-clock time close to the slowest single call instead of the sum of all nine.</p>

<h2>5. Components &amp; Workflow</h2>

<h3>The Nine Endpoints</h3>

<ol>
  <li>
    <p><strong>Endpoint:</strong> POST /v1/seo/meta-audit</p>
    <p><strong>What It Checks:</strong> Title tag, meta description, H1, canonical, robots meta (indexability), viewport, OpenGraph, and likely soft-404s</p>
    <p><strong>Why It Matters:</strong> 68% of pages with missing or duplicate titles lose click-through rate. Google uses the meta description as a snippet source 37% of the time.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p><strong>Endpoint:</strong> POST /v1/seo/broken-links-audit</p>
    <p><strong>What It Checks:</strong> Outbound and internal links returning 4xx/5xx, connection errors, timeouts</p>
    <p><strong>Why It Matters:</strong> Broken links waste crawl budget and degrade user trust. A single 404 on a product page can cost a conversion.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p><strong>Endpoint:</strong> POST /v1/seo/redirect-chain-map</p>
    <p><strong>What It Checks:</strong> Full redirect chain from initial URL to final destination, including intermediate hops</p>
    <p><strong>Why It Matters:</strong> Chains longer than 3 hops dilute link equity by 10–15% per hop. Chains with loops or broken intermediates cause indexation failures.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p><strong>Endpoint:</strong> POST /v1/seo/anchor-text-audit</p>
    <p><strong>What It Checks:</strong> Internal and external anchor text distribution, exact-match vs branded vs generic ratios</p>
    <p><strong>Why It Matters:</strong> Over-optimized anchor text profiles trigger Penguin. Under-optimized profiles miss ranking signals.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p><strong>Endpoint:</strong> POST /v1/seo/keyword-extract</p>
    <p><strong>What It Checks:</strong> TextRank-based keyword and keyphrase extraction from page content</p>
    <p><strong>Why It Matters:</strong> Identifies what the page is actually about vs what you think it's about. Gap analysis against target keywords.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p><strong>Endpoint:</strong> POST /v1/seo/readability</p>
    <p><strong>What It Checks:</strong> Flesch Reading Ease, Flesch-Kincaid Grade, Gunning Fog, SMOG and other grade-level scores, plus word, sentence, and reading-time counts. It scores text you send, so pass it the page text.</p>
    <p><strong>Why It Matters:</strong> Google's helpful content system favors readable content. Pages written above a grade 12 level see 23% lower engagement.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p><strong>Endpoint:</strong> POST /v1/seo/mixed-content</p>
    <p><strong>What It Checks:</strong> HTTP resources (images, scripts, iframes, fonts) loaded on HTTPS pages</p>
    <p><strong>Why It Matters:</strong> Mixed content triggers browser warnings and can break page rendering. Google may rank HTTPS pages lower if mixed content is present.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p><strong>Endpoint:</strong> POST /v1/seo/schema-validate</p>
    <p><strong>What It Checks:</strong> JSON-LD syntax, required properties for each recognized schema.org type, and which rich-result types the page is eligible for</p>
    <p><strong>Why It Matters:</strong> Valid schema increases rich-result eligibility by 3x. Invalid schema is ignored entirely — no error, no rich result.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p><strong>Endpoint:</strong> POST /v1/seo/snippet-candidates</p>
    <p><strong>What It Checks:</strong> Paragraph, list, and table blocks shaped like featured snippets</p>
    <p><strong>Why It Matters:</strong> 42% of search clicks go to the featured snippet. If your content isn't snippet-shaped, you can't win the position-zero slot.</p>
  </li>
</ol>

<h3>Workflow: One Audit Cycle</h3>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Seed URL list</strong> — Start with your sitemap, a list of priority pages, or a single homepage.</li>
  <li><strong>Parallel dispatch</strong> — Fire all nine endpoints simultaneously for each URL. Use asyncio or Promise.all to avoid sequential waits.</li>
  <li><strong>Collect responses</strong> — Gather each endpoint's JSON response for the page.</li>
  <li><strong>Aggregate results</strong> — Merge the JSON responses into a single audit document.</li>
  <li><strong>Score &amp; prioritize</strong> — Apply your own scoring logic or use Ollagraph's built-in grades.</li>
  <li><strong>Alert or report</strong> — Push results to a dashboard, send Slack alerts for critical failures, or file tickets in your issue tracker.</li>
</ul>

